wry documentation: ipc_handler with_html — ### Handle Key Presses with Event Listener

Source: https://github.com/tauri-apps/wry/blob/dev/examples/custom_protocol/index.html

Adds an event listener to the document's body to capture key presses. When a key is pressed, the event listener appends the pressed key to the innerHTML of an element with the ID 'keypresses'.

```javascript
document.body.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => { document.querySelector("#keypresses").innerHTML += " " + event.key; });
```

