### Create Child WebView with winit

Source: https://github.com/tauri-apps/wry/blob/dev/README.md

Illustrates creating a WebView as a child within another window using wry and winit. This example sets specific bounds for the child webview and demonstrates its integration into the application lifecycle.

```rust
use wry::{WebViewBuilder, WebView};
use winit::event_loop::{ActiveEventLoop, EventLoop};
use winit::window::{Window, WindowEvent};
use winit::dpi::{LogicalPosition, LogicalSize};
use wry::Rect;

#[derive(Default)]
struct App {
 window: Option<Window>,
 webview: Option<WebView>,
}

impl winit::application::ApplicationHandler for App {
 fn resumed(&mut self, event_loop: &ActiveEventLoop) {
 let window = event_loop.create_window(Window::default_attributes()).unwrap();
 let webview = WebViewBuilder::new()
 .with_url("https://tauri.app")
 .with_bounds(Rect {
 position: LogicalPosition::new(100, 100).into(),
 size: LogicalSize::new(200, 200).into(),
 })
 .build_as_child(&window)
 .unwrap();

 self.window = Some(window);
 self.webview = Some(webview);
 }

 fn window_event(&mut self, _event_loop: &ActiveEventLoop, _window_id: winit::window::WindowId, event: WindowEvent) {
 // Handle window events if necessary
 }
}

fn main() {
 let event_loop = EventLoop::new().unwrap();
 let mut app = App::default();
 event_loop.run_app(&mut app).unwrap();
}
```

